  "delta_effective_policy": "Profile candidate fields override the base v0.8 defaults. A candidate without response_caps uses its declared linear gain*amplitude*D; a bounded candidate applies tanh caps. Existing beta/tau/kappa structural transforms consume the resulting delta_effective.",
  "calibration_protocol_sha256": "48d65ccfb98a9f1c5bcd2ba52572db99318d2ffb96d3db9ef7d924265bbe15e6",
  "channel_transform": "D = sum fixed_budget * enabled_multiplier * R * unit_relation_vector. A bounded candidate uses c_j = cap_j*tanh(gain*amplitude_j*D_j/cap_j). The optional eta damping is a fixed bounded function of total D norm. Existing positive/negative axis guard transforms then apply.",
  "profile_policy": "Candidate selection uses all seven fixed canonical nodes and same point/short-period classifier; a candidate must be no worse in point/all-node-simple/default-node-simple counts and improve both mean world and centered RMS-normalized dayun Hellinger distances by at least 5%. Eligible maximum geometric mean ratio wins; fixed order ties. Otherwise v0.8 fallback.",
  "limits": "Finite canonical calibration does not prove complex shapes for arbitrary dates/inputs or all control values. Same ODE, initial state, burn, and world projection. Input budget ordering is not a guarantee of geometric effect ordering."
